  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strategic Assistance for Emergency Response in Democratic Republic of Congo (SAFER III)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since November 2019, Mercy Corps, Norwegian Refugee Council (NRC), ACTED, Solidarit&#xe9;s International (SI), and Concern Worldwide have united as one consortium to deliver Strategic Assistance for Emergency Response (SAFER) in the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC), a joint programme to harmonise emergency response among humanitarian actors in DRC, with the overall goal of enabling households affected by conflict and shocks  to  cover  their  basic  needs.  The  programme  supports  the  specific  outcome  of  delivering  a coordinated  humanitarian  response  that  enables  vulnerable  households  affected  by  conflict  and  shocks  to have safe and equitable access to multi-sectoral emergency assistance to reduce reliance  on  negative  coping  mechanisms.  This  is  achieved  through  the  provision  of  multi-sectoral  market-based Cash and Voucher Assistance or in-kind assistance and complementary Water, Sanitation and Hygiene services to meet the basic needs of conflict and shock-affected populations.</narrative>
  </description>
